# 03. NEW ART DIRECTION

## Contemporary Global Affairs Magazine

The new visual identity should combine:

1. Premium international news magazine.
2. Modern editorial art direction.
3. High-quality visual journalism.
4. Evidence-driven intelligence research.
5. Excellent digital reading UX.

The old archival-paper foundation can remain part of the brand, but it must no longer dictate every layout.

The product needs more contrast, stronger composition, greater visual variety, and more memorable imagery.

## 3.1 Visual personality

The intended personality:

- Intelligent.
- Confident.
- Contemporary.
- International.
- Editorial.
- Serious.
- Visually expressive.
- Refined.
- Trustworthy.

Avoid a cold administrative appearance.

Avoid the generic AI SaaS aesthetic.

Avoid a website where everything is beige, gray, white, and separated by tiny lines.

## 3.2 Avoid these design patterns

Explicitly avoid:

- Generic dashboard layouts.
- Repetitive three-column cards.
- Excessive thin borders.
- Repeated title / metadata / horizontal rule / paragraph patterns.
- Tiny monochrome metadata everywhere.
- Decorative radial SVG diagrams used for every story.
- Unnecessary rounded containers.
- Random gradients.
- Generic glassmorphism.
- Empty decorative graphics.
- Overly restrained visual hierarchy.
- Stock photography used without editorial context.
- The same hero layout on every edition.

Minimal design is acceptable.

Visual emptiness is not.

